    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0712" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg624"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scruggs to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic">September 24,
                        1892</hi></date>. (Received September 24.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Scruggs reports that the situation remains unchanged, nothing new having
                    occurred, and transmits a request of the Government of Venezuela that the
                    steamer <hi rendition="#italic">South Portland</hi>, laden with munitions of war
                    in New York, be prevented from entering Puerto Cabello by the naval forces of
                    the United States.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
